    keywords: ["Reflection", "Projection", "Self-awareness", "Truth"],
    meaning: `What is irritating you most about someone else right now? What in another person makes you recoil, feel threatened, or quietly furious? Look closer. The Mirror is not a comfortable card. It asks you to consider the possibility that what you see most clearly in others — both the qualities you admire and the ones you judge — are reflections of something alive in you. The person who frustrates you with their neediness may be showing you your own unmet needs. The one whose confidence unsettles you may be mirroring an unlived boldness you've been suppressing. This is not blame. It is the most radical form of self-knowledge available to you. The world is your mirror. And what it's reflecting right now contains information about where your greatest growth lies.`,
    affirmation: "Every reflection teaches me something true. I meet what I see with curiosity, not judgment.",
