    keywords: ["Shadow work", "Integration", "Hidden self", "Wholeness"],
    meaning: `The part of you that you are most ashamed of — the one that wants too much, feels too fiercely, acts in ways that contradict your self-image — that part has not gone anywhere just because you stopped looking at it. Your shadow is not your enemy. It is the exiled parts of yourself that never got to be whole, the instincts and desires and wounds that were told they were too much, too dark, too inconvenient. This card appears when those exiled parts are pressing against the door. Not to destroy you, but to be integrated. The most dangerous shadow is the one left in the dark, because it acts through you without your awareness. Turn toward it. Name what you find. The strange alchemy of shadow work is this: the thing you feared most in yourself, once met with honest eyes, loses its power to control you — and sometimes becomes your greatest gift.`,
    affirmation: "I turn toward my shadow with courage. In integration, I become fully whole.",
